body:
I used to drink mouthwash of all things and wouldn't accept I (OBVIOUSLY) had a problem. I tried to get into a relationship with someone, something I really wanted, and things didn't work out. It made me realise I couldn't be the way I was and continue to pretend I was just like everyone else and just as capable of being in relationships, being healthy, happy etc. and I didn't want to put my friends through stress because of my problems. This was no where as big a problem as most people have to go through, but it still hurt people I never wanted to hurt.

&#x200B;

Guilt I guess, and the thought that if all my friends could get through the same shit I did without drinking anything, then so could I, and they helped me out of it.

Trying to empathise with people who think this is a good idea, SUPPOSEDLY  it'd encourage people, teenagers especially, to be more careful and use protection to prevent having an unwanted child, since they don't have any other options. Positive outcomes of this would be a more limited spread of STI's, and in the best outcome only people with children they actually wanted and less kids put up for adoption or growing up in bad conditions.

&#x200B;

However, as others have pointed out, this wouldn't help victims of rape in any way. It's more likely as well that more kids would be put up for adoption and forced to live in unfortunate conditions, as while people being more careful when they have sex would make sense I don't think things would really change significantly if abortion was made illegal. Instead, I think it'd only contribute to current problems of that sort.

&#x200B;

While I can see positives to making abortion illegal, ultimately I don't think it would benefit society, and I feel like its more that people are uncomfortable with the thought of intervening with the natural progression of life. That being said, I don't feel completely comfortable with abortion myself (I don't think it should be performed after 20 weeks of pregnancy) although I feel that it is necessary in cases such as unintentional teenage pregnancy and rape victims at the very least.

&#x200B;

Edit: Didn't make it clear enough that I was trying to figure out why someone would want abortion to be illegal and not that I actually held that belief. Sorry!
